# Python Backend Rules

Use:
- Python 3.11 or 3.12
- FastAPI
- Pydantic
- SQLAlchemy
- PostgreSQL
- Redis
- ib_insync for IBKR integration unless replaced later
- pytest for tests

Code requirements:
- type hints required
- no hardcoded secrets
- use environment variables
- use Pydantic models for API payloads
- return structured JSON responses
- log every trading decision
- never silently fail
- never bypass risk checks

API endpoints should live under:
trading-engine/app/api/

Business logic should live under:
trading-engine/app/scanner/
trading-engine/app/features/
trading-engine/app/models/
trading-engine/app/risk/
trading-engine/app/execution/
trading-engine/app/storage/

Do not place broker execution logic directly inside route handlers.
Routes call services. Services call risk gate. Risk gate calls execution only when approved.
